y, a roughly nine-to-one financial advantage, and a Likely D consensus among raters and markets in a district that only leans modestly Democratic. The absence of polling and active Republican outside spending argue for a solid but not overwhelming edge.", "watch": "Sustained House Republican advertising on Long Island, if paired with a strong national environment, could pull the margin into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laura Gillen (D) is running."]}, "overview": "New York's 4th District leans slightly Democratic, and incumbent Laura Gillen enters the general election with a commanding financial edge, having raised roughly nine times as much as Republican Jeanine Driscoll and holding a large cash-on-hand advantage. Expert ratings cluster around Likely D, with several outlets rating the race Safe or Solid D, and prediction markets price her chances around 90 to 94 percent.\n\nNo public polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals. Driscoll cleared her primary but has minimal resources, while national Republican groups have reserved television ads targeting Gillen on Long Island. The district's narrow partisan lean keeps the seat within reach in a strong Republican year, but the weight of evidence points to a Gillen hold by a solid, though not overwhelming, margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9622, "margin": 11.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9401, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9422, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9272, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9344, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9323, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9413, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9576, "margin": 1